Define project objectives – Clearly identify what the project aims to achieve.

Define project scope – Determine what is included and excluded from the project.

Create a work breakdown structure (WBS) – Divide the project into smaller tasks and activities.

Prepare a schedule – Set timelines, milestones, and deadlines for each task.

Allocate resources – Identify the people, tools, technology, materials, and budget required.

Assign responsibilities – Decide who is responsible for each task.

Estimate the budget – Calculate the expected project costs.

Identify risks – Determine possible problems and prepare mitigation strategies.

Set milestones – Define important checkpoints to measure project progress.

Define communication methods – Decide how team members and stakeholders will share updates and information.
